21.3.1  \tfrac{x^2}{\eta^2+\xi^2-1}=f^2; \tfrac{\eta^2}{\eta^2}\dfrac{y^2}{1-\eta^2}=f^2
z=r\cos\phi; x=r\sin\phi; 0\leq\phi\leq2\pi
where k, n and e are oblate spheroidal coordinates.
Relations Between Cartesian and Oblate Spheroidal Coordinates
